Subject: [PATCH] docs(r48c): close the Fable LOW gates - measured registry
 rows, corrected coverage and failure-signature claims

Documentation only apart from one test comment.

- docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md: GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_XFOLD and GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_MMVQ rows
  re-written from UNMEASURED to the measured pairing (3 quiet interleaved rounds,
  one binary env-flipped). XFOLD: n=1..5,7,8 wash -3.0..+5.6%, n=6 +26..+38%,
  no q6_K row below -3%; acceptance rule 1 recorded as NOT met (ffn-gate-up
  +3.69%). MMVQ: wash/+5% at n<=4 on ffn-down/legacy (but -3.28% n=1 and -12.11%
  n=4 on embd-out), -46..-143% at n>=5, DIAGNOSTIC, default stays f32.
  GGML_VK_Q6K_DIRECT_SCALES row: serve bit-identity re-run marked OWED.
- report 10.3: "all-zero or partially-stale destination (ERR 1.0, 0.997, 0.055
  observed)"; the "exactly 1.0 on every failure" absolutism is gone.
- report 10.1 / 10.4 / 10.7 / 10.8: cite the checker's 42-* (pure-upstream path
  3/60) and 40-* (S-X8 same shape and z-split 0/60); state the narrowed lead as
  the Q6_K host path, not the z-split geometry alone.
- report 4 / 8 / 10.8: the protected win's serve-level byte-identity between the
  DIRECT_SCALES arms on the new shader is OWED to HQ and runs as a load-only
  deterministic cell in the R48 integration gates. No model was run here.
- report 6: acceptance outcome table - rule 1 NOT met, keep rests on rule 2
  (worst -2.97%) plus the n=6 dip removal (+38.0/+27.5/+26.3%, arm A 31.1 GB/s
  at n=6 against 67.2 at n=5).
- f16 src1 coverage claim corrected in report 4, new report 8 item 8, and the
  test comment at tests/test-backend-ops.cpp: the 8 q6_K/f16 rows are declined by
  the CPU reference ("not supported [CPU]", 0 OK), so mul_mat_vec_q6_k_f16_f32 is
  UNCOVERED. Rows kept, claim withdrawn.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-236 R48c gates, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - documentation and coverage-claim corrections after independent check
